The dataset exhibited an imbalanced class distribution, with 602 instances belonging to class 0 (“not engaged”), 372 to class 1 (“neutral”), and 624 to class 2 (“engaged”). To mitigate potential bias toward majority classes without artificially modifying the empirical distribution of samples, a cost sensitive learning strategy based on per-sample weighting was adopted. For each training split, class-specific weights were computed according to the balanced formulation:5\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
