Balanced accuracy was computed as the average recall across classes:\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
                                                  \usepackage{amsmath}
                                                  \usepackage{wasysym}
                                                  \usepackage{amsfonts}
                                                  \usepackage{amssymb}
                                                  \usepackage{amsbsy}
                                                  \usepackage{mathrsfs}
                                                  \usepackage{upgreek}
                                                  \setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
                                                  \begin{document}$$Balanced accuracy=\frac{1}{C}\sum_{C=1}^{C}{Recall}_{C}$$\end{document}where C is the number of classes. Macro-averaged metrics were obtained by computing the metric independently for each class and then averaging across classes, assigning equal weight to each class. Weighted-averaged metrics were computed by averaging class-wise scores according to the number of samples in each class.
